dress><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIMOTO KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKITA HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO SHIGEAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA YASUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARADA, HISASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANAYAMA, RYOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANETO, KIMIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASUNO, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, TAKEHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORI, KUNIYASU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ONO, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIMOTO, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKITA, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, SHIGEAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, YASUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for separating a green sand mold and an as-cast product which comprises surrounding gas-tightly a green sand mold without a mold flask having been supplied with a melt and aspirating steeply the inside of a structure surrounding the sand mold gas-tightly so as to reduce the pressure thereof to a pressure of -200 mmHg as expressed in gauge pressure or less within a period of 0.5 seconds and to a pressure of -360 mmHg or less finally, thereby reducing the boiling temperature of the water being present within the whole green sand mold including a condensed water layer formed around the as-cast product in the green sand mold, to bring this water to boil, which results in the break of the green sand mold and in the separation from the as-cast product. After the break of the sand mold, the above structure is brought back to an ordinary pressure and the as-cast product is taken out. The method can be used for securing the separation of an as-cast product from a green sand mold and the break of the green sand mold.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de séparation d'un moule en sable vert d'un produit brut de coulée. Ledit procédé consiste à entourer, d'une manière étanche aux gaz, un moule en sable vert sans châssis de moule contenant une matière fondue, et à aspirer fortement l'intérieur d'une structure entourant, d'une manière étanche aux gaz, le moule en sable vert de façon à ramener sa pression à une pression de 200 mmHg exprimée en pression effective ou inférieure dans un intervalle de 0,5 seconde, et à une pression de 360 mmHg ou inférieure. La température d'ébullition de l'eau est ainsi réduite dans l'ensemble du moule en sable vert, y compris la couche d'eau condensée formée autour du produit brut de coulée dans ledit moule, et, enfin, à amener l'eau à ébullition, le résultat étant que le moule en sable vert se brise et se sépare du produit brut de coulée. Après la cassure du moule en sable, la structure ci-dessus est ramenée à une pression ordinaire et le produit brut de coulée évacué. On peut utiliser le procédé pour assurer la séparation d'un produit brut de coulée d'un moule en sable vert et la cassure de ce dernier.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>